// Keyes KY-019, the red 1-channel board in Arduino starter kits.
// https://arduinomodules.info/ky-019-5v-relay-module/ names the Songle SRD-05VDC-SL-C,
// the S8050, the 1N4007 and the indicator LED, and says the coil current comes from
// VCC. The board is active high: IN high turns the relay on.
//
// The two resistors on that board are marked 102, which is 1 kohm. IN goes through
// one to the S8050 base. The emitter is GND. The collector is the coil, and the
// other coil pin is VCC. The 1N4007 sits across the coil with its cathode at VCC.
// The LED and the other 1 kohm sit from VCC to the collector, so the LED lights
// while IN is high and VCC is up. A drawing that puts 1 Mohm in the base and swaps
// the transistor cannot drive this coil, and this model does not follow it.
//
// The header stands on one edge of the board with its pins pointing up, for female
// jumpers. The screw terminal is on the opposite edge, COM in the middle, with its wire
// entries facing out. The board does not plug into a breadboard. It lies beside one,
// wired with jumpers.
